# Do NOT ignore dist/fezoctl.mjs or skills/*/scripts/fezoctl.mjs. BOTH copies
# of the bundle are committed deliberately.
#
# The skill-local copy is what makes the skill directory self-contained, and a
# self-contained skill directory is what installers like `npx skills add` need:
# they copy `skills/<name>/` recursively out of the repo tree and nothing else,
# so tier 3 of the invocation ladder (`$SKILL_DIR/../../dist/fezoctl.mjs`)
# cannot resolve at the install target and tier 2 is the only rung left. Ignore
# the copy and every such install ships a SKILL.md with no engine.
#
# The two files are byte-identical, so git stores ONE blob for both paths.
# Committing the copy costs a tree entry, not a second bundle.
